From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Subject: [PATCH] VideoInfoScanner: scrape new movies of a folder four at a time

A library scan scraped one movie after the other, ~2.6 s each on S928X
(TMDB search + details in two languages + collection + fanart.tv, python
start-up, stream details with a decoded HDR frame). The new plain movie files
of a directory listing are now fetched ahead on 4 threads (search, details,
stream details); the serial loop picks the results up in order, so everything
that touches the library stays serial. Each thread uses its own database
connection and scraper instance. Nfo, identifiers in filenames, stacks and
discs still go the serial way, and a result is only used when it searched for
the same title and year the serial path would.

Two things had to change for concurrent runs of one scraper:
- CScriptInvocationManager: the reusable invoker is checked and taken in
  separate steps, so threads running the same reusable script at once (the
  TMDB scraper has reuselanguageinvoker) got the same invoker and plugin handle
  and each other's results (one movie got another's details). A thread-local
  flag makes the scanner threads use one-off invokers.
- CPythonInvoker: sub-interpreters are created and ended one at a time (a
  crash in PyEval_RestoreThread with four starting at once).

Measured on S928X: 108 movies in 114 s (was ~280 s), titles identical file by
file to the serial scan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
